Playdate
--------

.. contents::

About
-----

Playdate is a plugin for Geany that brings the `Panic Playdate
<https://play.date>`_ handheld game development workflow into the
editor: compile with ``pdc``, run the result in the Playdate
Simulator, and jump to compiler errors from Geany's Compiler tab.

It also installs optional Geany tags for the Playdate Lua API so
autocomplete and call tips work for ``playdate.*`` symbols.


Features
--------

* **Build** — runs ``$SDK/bin/pdc <source> <output>``
* **Build and Run** — build, then launch the Playdate Simulator
* **Run in Simulator** — open the existing ``.pdx`` bundle
* **Clean** — remove the generated ``.pdx`` output directory
* **Open Simulator** — start the Simulator without building
* **Compiler tab integration** — ``pdc`` ``warning:`` / ``error:``
  lines become clickable messages (``file:line``)
* **Preferences** — SDK path, source directory, output ``.pdx``,
  product name and ``pdc`` flags (``-s``, ``--no-compress``, ``-v``,
  ``-q``, ``-k``)
* **API tags** — Tools → Playdate → Install API Tags installs
  ~1800 tags generated from
  `playdate-luacats <https://github.com/notpeter/playdate-luacats>`_
* **Keybindings** — Build and Run on ``F5`` by default (rebindable)

Command shapes follow
`orta/vscode-playdate <https://github.com/orta/vscode-playdate>`_ and
`midouest/vscode-playdate-debug
<https://github.com/midouest/vscode-playdate-debug>`_.


Requirements
------------

* Geany >= 1.26 (tested with 2.1, GTK3)
* Playdate SDK from https://play.date/dev/ (``pdc`` + Simulator)

On Linux the simulator binary is ``PlaydateSimulator``. On macOS and
Windows the paths differ; the plugin currently focuses on Linux.


Usage
-----

1. Install the Playdate SDK and either export ``PLAYDATE_SDK_PATH``
   or set the SDK path in the plugin preferences.
2. Open a file inside a Playdate project. The project root is the
   directory that *contains* ``Source/`` or ``source/``:

   ::

       MyGame/
       ├── source/          (or Source/)
       │   ├── main.lua
       │   └── pdxinfo
       └── MyGame.pdx/      (output)

3. Use Tools → Playdate → **Build and Run** (or ``F5``).
4. Compiler messages appear in the Compiler tab; double-click jumps
   to the file and line.
5. Optionally run **Install API Tags** and restart Geany to get
   Playdate Lua autocomplete.

Empty Source/Output fields in preferences mean auto-detect.


Development
-----------

Source lives in the combined geany-plugins repository::

    git clone https://github.com/geany/geany-plugins.git
    cd geany-plugins
    ./autogen.sh --enable-playdate
    make

Standalone development repository:
https://github.com/davi19/geany-playdate


Known issues
------------

* Simulator launch and path detection currently target Linux.
* Large embedded API tag data (``tags_data.h``) makes the object file
  larger than typical plugins.

Please report issues at
https://github.com/geany/geany-plugins/issues


